        <h1>November 28 in Music History: The 1970s Number Ones</h1>

        <p class="post-byline">By <a href="https://musicofthe70s.net/about/author/">Charlie</a> &middot; Published {{DATE_LONG}}</p>
        <p class="jump-to-list"><a class="btn-primary jump-btn" href="#november-28-list">&#9654; Jump to the playable list</a></p>

        <p class="post-intro">On November 28 in music history, the number one song in America changed with every year of the 1970s.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">The Billboard Hot 100 chart week that contains November 28 had a different song on top in all ten years.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">Those ten songs spent {{TOTAL_WEEKS}} weeks at number one between them.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">You can play every one from the table below.</p>
        <p class="post-intro">Each row also shows how far into its run the song was that week.</p>

