            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/That%27s_the_Way_(I_Like_It)" rel="noopener">That's the Way (I Like It), Wikipedia</a>, for the writers, the album and the two separate weeks at number one.</li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonight%27s_the_Night_(Gonna_Be_Alright)" rel="noopener">Tonight's the Night (Gonna Be Alright), Wikipedia</a>, for the writer, the producer, the eight weeks at number one and the French spoken part.</li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You_Light_Up_My_Life_(song)" rel="noopener">You Light Up My Life (song), Wikipedia</a>, for the ten-week record, the writer and the awards.</li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacArthur_Park_(song)" rel="noopener">MacArthur Park (song), Wikipedia</a>, for the writer, the producers and Donna Summer's three weeks at number one.</li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_More_Tears_(Enough_Is_Enough)" rel="noopener">No More Tears (Enough Is Enough), Wikipedia</a>, for the writers, the producers and the first-duet-by-two-women note.</li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100" rel="noopener">Billboard Hot 100, Wikipedia</a>, for how the weekly chart used for number one runs works.</li>
